   "key": "similar",
   "title": "Diseases that share biology",
   "text": "A paper reports that the brain cell connection problems seen in Rett syndrome, called synaptic dysfunction, are discussed together with a condition named Fragile X syndrome, because both show changes in how synapses work [E53e2c3c]. This means the two conditions may share some of the same underlying biology at the level of brain cell connections [Ee884043, E53e2c3c]. It may be worth asking the care team whether research on this shared mechanism is relevant to your child [E53e2c3c].",
